## SUBAGENTS AND PARALLEL WORK

If your runtime provides subagents or a parallel-task mechanism, fan out
independent read-only checks across plan compliance, security, correctness,
performance, maintainability, and test coverage. Give each subagent a distinct
scope, then reconcile its concrete evidence yourself. If no such mechanism is
available, perform the same checks sequentially. Only the main session may decide
the verdict, submit the `issues` artifact, or declare completion.

Bring fresh evidence the implementation phase did not have, read recorded assumptions, and compare the changed files against the plan and requirements. Return only material findings with their concrete cost and exact fix; `no_issues` is a normal result.

Grade the change on these review dimensions, which the downstream judge also reads: plan compliance, security, correctness, performance, maintainability, and test coverage. Record a specific not-applicable reason under `## Review Evidence` for a dimension with no relevant surface. Run the project's fast path before broader verification when one exists, then run the meaningful full gate; do not rely on the diff's claims.

