Submit review findings using `artifact_type="issues"`.

The downstream artifact validator reads this grammar: `.agent/artifact-formats/issues.md`. Submit `type: issues` with status `no_issues` or `issues_found`.

- `## Summary`: exactly one item.
- `## Review Evidence`: `dimension or requirement | concrete evidence`; include one item per applicable review dimension and one item per plan requirement and acceptance criterion.
- For `issues_found`, add non-empty `## Issues` (`path | high|medium|low | summary`), `## What Came Up Short`, and `## How To Fix` sections with concrete evidence and executable remediation.
- When `status` is `no_issues`, `## Review Evidence` must be non-empty; omit those three remediation sections.

{% set issues_example %}
---
type: issues
status: no_issues
---

## Summary
- [SUM-1] The implementation is correct and verification passed.

## Review Evidence
- [E-1] Plan compliance | Every plan requirement and acceptance criterion maps to an inspected implementation or verification result.
- [E-2] Security | Input, secret, permission, and command boundaries in the changed surface were inspected with no defect found.
- [E-3] Correctness | Error paths and adversarial edge cases were exercised by focused tests.
- [E-4] Performance | The change adds no unbounded work or blocking operation; the bounded startup path was verified.
- [E-5] Maintainability | New helpers have one owner, no dead compatibility branch, and accurate documentation.
- [E-6] Test coverage | Focused regressions cover the new behavior and independent near-miss cases.
- [E-7] Acceptance criterion AC-1 | The criterion is demonstrated by the named focused test and inspected runtime path.
{% endset %}
Example issues artifact when the implementation needs fixes:

```markdown
---
type: issues
status: issues_found
---

## Summary
- [SUM-1] The feature works in the happy path, but error handling and regression coverage are incomplete.

## Review Evidence
- [E-1] Plan compliance | The error-handling requirement is not satisfied in ralph/pipeline/runner.py.
- [E-2] Test coverage | tests/test_runner.py has no malformed-output regression case.

## Issues
- [I-1] ralph/pipeline/runner.py | high | A failure path still treats runtime text as markup.
- [I-2] tests/test_runner.py | medium | Coverage is missing for the malformed-output error path.

## What Came Up Short
- [W-1] ralph/pipeline/runner.py still has one failure output path that renders runtime text unsafely.
- [W-2] There is no regression test proving malformed tool output cannot crash the remaining CLI error output path.

## How To Fix
- [F-1] Convert the remaining CLI failure output path to a Rich Text-based render so runtime strings are always treated as literal text.
- [F-2] Add a regression test that feeds bracket-heavy runtime text through the affected path and confirms rendering does not raise MarkupError.
```

